From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:09:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] flashnext: pr_check clean and the layout tests re-pinned
 on the 64-row branch

The branch now passes upstream's own gate: every comment it adds is a
single line under 120 columns (the probe explanation, the max_rows and
served_rows docblocks, the window-check notes, the fused kernel's log
rule), with the mechanics in the receipt and the PR body. The
CHANGELOG gains an Unreleased bullet; its number is the placeholder
the gate checks and becomes the real PR number when the PR opens.

The draft layout tests hardcode the window's row counts, which the
wider max_rows doubles: the scores, saved-projection and n-gram-row
terms now derive from max_rows and the pinned totals are the suite's
own measured values (a 65,536-token draft is 411,436,032 bytes full
and 315,737,088 half; the saved pieces 79,646,720 and 40,570,880; the
half-head stream 1,430,615,040 with its caches).

lean 116 vs 116 (0 new), pr_check 0 errors 0 warnings, zig fmt clean,
and the host suite's failure set is origin/main's own three (listener,
two drama voice tools, environmental without a GPU in the container).
